  "body": "Make worktrees the default working mode so the `main` checkout stays clean and ready to receive merges.\n\n## Why\n`AGENTS.md` already said \"prefer small reviewable PRs, do not push straight to main,\" but it had no concrete mechanism for keeping `main` clean. Sessions that touched feature branches often showed `.worktrees/` as untracked in the `main` checkout, and a worktree lived in the in-repo path for the duration of PR 14.\n\n## What\n- **AGENTS.md** (Working style): agents must work in a worktree, not the `main` checkout. Default location is outside the repo at `../worktrees/<branch-slug>`, with the worktree-add command shown verbatim.\n- **AGENTS.md** (Repo conventions): keep `main` clean; retire worktrees with `git worktree remove`.\n- **.gitignore**: add `.worktrees/` as a safety net for agents that use the in-repo path.\n- **scripts/review.sh**: refuse to run from `main` unless `REVIEW_MODE=docs`; the error message points the agent at the worktree-add command.\n- **tests/test_readme.py**: assert the new AGENTS.md guidance and the `.worktrees/` ignore line.\n- **tests/test_app.py**: new `ReviewScriptGuardTests` class exercises the guard with a stubbed `git` binary, so the test stays self-contained and doesn't recurse into the suite it is testing.\n\n## Verified\n- `uv run python -m unittest tests.test_app tests.test_readme` → 31/31 OK\n- `uv run python -m py_compile app.py scripts/snapshot_dashboard.py` → clean\n- `scripts/review.sh` from this branch → \"Full review mode complete\"\n- Guard check (run guarded `scripts/review.sh` from `main` in full mode) → exit 1 with the expected error message pointing at `git worktree add ../worktrees/<branch-slug> -b <branch> origin/main`\n- Same call from `main` with `REVIEW_MODE=docs` → exit 0\n\n## Out of scope\n- Removing the existing in-repo worktree at `.worktrees/review-pr-14`. It pre-dates this rule and will be retired by the user separately.",
  "changed_files": 5,
